<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/E (C programming is a powerful, general-purpose, and procedural programming language widely used for system-level and application development. Known for its simplicity and efficiency, C provides low- level access to memory and a rich set of built-in functions, making it ideal for developing operating systems, embedded systems, and software requiring high performance. Its modular approach, using functions and structures, enables code reusability and scalability. Though it lacks advanced features like object-oriented programming, C remains a foundational language, forming the basis of many modern programming languages and serving as an excellent tool for understanding core programming concepts.)
/Pg 20 0 R
/K [3]
>>
