301 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/E (These specify what the system should do. The key functions of a food delivery system may include:1. *User Registration & Authentication:* - Users can create accounts by providing necessary details \(name, email, phone number, etc.\). - Users can log in to their account securely using a username and password. 2. *Menu Display:* - The system should display the list of available food items, categorized into various sections \(e.g., appetizers, main course, drinks, desserts\). - Each food item should display its name, description, price, and available quantity.3. *Order Placement:* - Users can select food items from the menu and add them to their cart. - Users can modify their cart by adding/removing items before checkout. - The system should calculate the total price, including applicable taxes and discounts.4. *Order Confirmation:* - Users should receive a confirmation of their order with details \(item names, quantity, price, and estimated delivery time\). 5. *Payment Processing:* - Users can pay for their order using different methods \(e.g., credit/debit card, digital wallets, cash on delivery\). - The system should process the payment securely and generate a payment receipt.6. *Order Tracking:* - Users should be able to track the status of their order in real-time \(e.g., placed, preparing, out for delivery, delivered\).7. *Delivery Management:* - The system should allow users to input their delivery address. - Delivery personnel can update the status of delivery, and users can view real-time updates. )
/Pg 21 0 R
/K [3]
>>
endobj
